THOUGHT: The NullAway error is about passing a @Nullable `str` to `deobfClassName`, which expects @NonNull. In `decodeAttribute`, `str` comes from `valuesParser.decodeValue`, which can be null (as evidenced by the later null check when writing it). To satisfy NullAway without changing behavior, I should guard the deobfuscation call with a null check so `deobfClassName` is only called when `str` is non-null. Next, I’ll edit the file to wrap `str = deobfClassName(str);` in an `if (str != null)` block, then run the compile to ensure the NullAway error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/jadx && sed -i '538,542s/if (isDeobfCandidateAttr(shortNsName, attrName)) {
				str = deobfClassName(str);
			}/if (isDeobfCandidateAttr(shortNsName, attrName) \&\& str != null) {
				str = deobfClassName(str);
			}/' jadx-core/src/main/java/jadx/core/xmlgen/BinaryXMLParser.java && ./gradlew jadx-core:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway:|error: \[NullAway\]" -n new_build_output.log | head || true```

